<title>USA: Teamsters to vote on UPS deal Tuesday.</title>
<headline>Teamsters to vote on UPS deal Tuesday.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Local leaders of the Teamsters union will meet in Washington late on Tuesday to vote on the tentative settlement with United Parcel Service, a union spokesman said.</p>
<p>&quot;The leaders of the local unions will come in and review the settlement and then vote on it,&quot; Jeff Cappella told Reuters. The meeting was set to start at 7 p.m. EDT (2300 GMT) at a Washington hotel.</p>
<p>&quot;After that it will be sent out to every UPS Teamsters member around the country to vote and ratify it. That process could take about a month,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>((Washington newsroom, 202 898-8300))</p>
